halui.machine.ui-disable takes estop and machine power away from the UIs, and
only from them.

A milltask that is one part of a machine network has its estop wired in
hardware, and the master switches it on and off.  The operator must not take
that part down from its screen by accident, so emccmd refuses every set_state
-- estop, estop reset, machine on and off -- while the pin is high, unless the
caller passes force.  Estop is refused too: the hardware chain is the estop.

What must keep working is checked as well: halui's machine and estop pins,
forced emccmd calls, and program flow, which has its own pin.

The pin is linked from the config's own HAL file to prove it exists by the
time that file runs.
